d. Drafting the plan now. If any worker node throws an unhandled exception, we abort the entire job and purge the output buffer.\\n\\n**[2026-06-12 10:43] Charlie**: I've added an exception hook to the core engine. It catches low-level segfaults and signals the controller to stop all active streams.\\n\\n**[2026-06-12 11:23] Bob**: Implementation complete. Added an atomic rename step at the very end — the output folder stays empty until the last file is verified.\\n\\n**[2026-06-12 12:53] Diana**: What about logs? We need to know *why* it failed.\\n\\n**[2026-06-12 13:16] Bob**: Crash report gets written to a separate `audit_log.json` before the shutdown. Captures the stack trace and the filename that triggered the fault.\\n\\n**[2026-06-12 13:17] Charlie**: Perfect. :lock:\\n\\n**[2026-06-12 13:19] Alice**: Thanks.\\n\\n**[2026-07-16 09:30] Diana**: QA pass on fail-closed is done — confirmed no output file gets written on failure and the temp files get securely deleted. Signing off before the encryption and offline work start relying on this.\\n\\n**[2026-07-16 09:31] Bob**: Calling this done.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src slack 12 slack thread batch failur strategi fail close channel cipherdoc thread open 2026 06 12 last activ 2026 07 16 2026 06 12 10 09 bob for the batch fail close question we need to decid what happen if the engin crash halfway through a1 000 file batch do we keep the success one 2026 06 12 10 26 charli absolut not if we can t guarante 100 of the batch is safe we should fail close no partial export 2026 06 12 10 28 bob agre draft the plan now if ani worker node throw an unhandl except we abort the entir job and purg the output buffer 2026 06 12 10 43 charli i ve ad an except hook to the core engin it catch low level segfault and signal the control to stop all activ stream 2026 06 12 11 23 bob implement complet ad an atom renam step at the veri end the output folder stay empti until the last file is verifi 2026 06 12 12 53 diana what about log we need to know whi it fail 2026 06 12 13 16 bob crash report get written to a separ audit _ log json befor the shutdown captur the stack trace and the filenam that trigger the fault 2026 06 12 13 17 charli perfect lock 2026 06 12 13 19 alic thank 2026 07 16 09 30 diana qa pas on fail close is done confirm no output file get written on failur and the temp file get secur delet sign off befor the encrypt and offlin work start reli on this 2026 07 16 09 31 bob call this done\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e906ce748a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-06-12-batch-failures.md\", \"id\": \"1313e24c5f4d4803\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.2969582077194814, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.11455374102783053, \"vector_similarity\": 0.72256863, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-06-12-batch-failures.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e906ce748a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-06-12-batch-failures.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-06-12-batch-failures.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1616, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:04:03\", \"token_count\": 478, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-04\\n\\n# OCR Fallback — Tesseract Proof of Concept\\n\\n**Owner**: Charlie\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2004\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-06-28\\n\\nTask T008 (OCR fallback for documents without a usable native text layer, WS-01) has reached a Tesseract-based proof of concept today.\\n\\n## What This Covers\\n\\nA POC path for routing documents with no usable native text layer through OCR instead, so the redaction pipeline still has text to run detection against.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-04\\n\\n# OCR Fallback — Tesseract Proof of Concept\\n\\n**Owner**: Charlie\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2004\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-06-28\\n\\nTask T008 (OCR fallback for documents without a usable native text layer, WS-01) has reached a Tesseract-based proof of concept today.\\n\\n## Status\\n\\nActive — POC only.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-04\\n\\n# OCR Fallback — Tesseract Proof of Concept\\n\\n**Owner**: Charlie\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2004\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-06-28\\n\\nTask T008 (OCR fallback for documents without a usable native text layer, WS-01) has reached a Tesseract-based proof of concept today.\\n\\n## Limitation\\n\\nThis is a proof of concept, not a production integration. Performance characteristics under real batch load and confidence-threshold behavior have not been evaluated yet.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-04\\n\\n# OCR Fallback — Tesseract Proof of Concept\\n\\n**Owner**: Charlie\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2004\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-06-28\\n\\nTask T008 (OCR fallback for documents without a usable native text layer, WS-01) has reached a Tesseract-based proof of concept today.\\n\\n## Next Step\\n\\nMove from POC toward integration with the rest of the scan pipeline; no timeline set yet.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src gdoc 04 ocr fallback tesseract proof of concept owner charli document key doc 2004 last updat 2026 06 28 task t008 ocr fallback for document without a usabl nativ text layer w 01 ha reach a tesseract base proof of concept today what this cover a poc path for rout document with no usabl nativ text layer through ocr instead so the redact pipelin still ha text to run detect against sourc id src gdoc 04 ocr fallback tesseract proof of concept owner charli document key doc 2004 last updat 2026 06 28 task t008 ocr fallback for document without a