dic for quarantin page an end to end quarantin test exercis the ui and metadata path but the 90 confid threshold integr is still in progress and the task remain activ clickup task ciph 24 sourc id src cu ciph 24 task id ciph 24 titl manual review threshold for low confid ocr status activ assigne diana prioriti normal date creat 2026 06 25 activ histori 2026 06 25 diana task creat open\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e959cb748a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/tasks/CIPH-24-Manual-Review-Threshold.md\", \"id\": \"33e745ef8511a565\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.2888611028649818, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.08708543266425978, \"vector_similarity\": 0.759671, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/tasks/CIPH-24-Manual-Review-Threshold.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e959cb748a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/tasks/CIPH-24-Manual-Review-Threshold.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/tasks/CIPH-24-Manual-Review-Threshold.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1286, \"chunk_count\": 2, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:02:57\", \"token_count\": 609, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-SLACK-11\\n\\n# Slack Thread: Manual Review Threshold Design\\n\\n**Channel**: #cipherdoc\\n\\n**Thread opened**: 2026-06-28\\n\\n**Last activity**: 2026-09-18\\n\\n---\\n\\n**[2026-06-28 09:08] Diana**: Starting on the manual review threshold work. We need a safety valve for when the engine isn't confident about a redaction. I'm proposing a 90% confidence threshold — anything below that gets flagged for manual review.\\n\\n**[2026-06-28 09:55] Charlie**: How do we define \\\"confidence\\\"? Just the regex match score, or are we factoring in OCR quality too?\\n\\n**[2026-06-28 10:09] Diana**: Both. If the OCR engine gives a low confidence score for a block of text, we should flag it regardless of the regex match.\\n\\n**[2026-08-06 10:49] Diana**: Picking this back up — implementing the quarantine folder now. Docs that fall below the 90% threshold land there and won't be exported until a human confirms the redaction.\\n\\n**[2026-08-20 13:35] Diana**: Quarantine folder alone doesn't give reviewers enough context. Designing the metadata that goes with each quarantined file: confidence score, page number, and the reason it was flagged.\\n\\n**[2026-09-05 14:34] Charlie**: Added visual indicators in the UI for quarantined pages, tied to that metadata, so reviewers can see at a glance why a page was held.\\n\\n**[2026-09-18 15:55] Diana**: Ran an end-to-end pass: detection -> quarantine -> metadata -> UI markers -> manual approval. The pipeline holds together, but the 90% threshold tuning itself is still in progress — I want another round of testing before I'd call it locked.\\n\\n**[2026-09-18 15:58] Charlie**: Makes sense. Let me know when you want another look at the UI side once the threshold settles.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src slack 11 slack thread manual review threshold design channel cipherdoc thread open 2026 06 28 last activ 2026 09 18 2026 06 28 09 08 diana start on the manual review threshold work we need a safeti valv for when the engin isn t confid about a redact i m propos a 90 confid threshold anyth below that get flag for manual review 2026 06 28 09 55 charli how do we defin confid just the regex match score or are we factor in ocr qualiti too 2026 06 28 10 09 diana both if the ocr engin give a low confid score for a block of text we should flag it regardless of the regex match 2026 08 06 10 49 diana pick this back up implement the quarantin folder now doc that fall below the 90 threshold land there and won t be export until a human confirm the redact 2026 08 20 13 35 diana quarantin folder alon doesn t give review enough context design the metadata that go with each quarantin file confid score page number and the reason it wa flag 2026 09 05 14 34 charli ad visual indic in the ui for quarantin page tie to that metadata so review can see at a glanc whi a page wa held 2026 09 18 15 55 diana ran an end to end pas detect quarantin metadata ui marker manual approv the pipelin hold togeth but the 90 threshold tune itself is still in progress i want anoth round of test befor i d call it lock 2026 09 18 15 58 charli make sens let me know when you want anoth look at the ui side onc the threshold settl\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e917c6d48a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-06-28-manual-review-threshold.md\", \"id\": \"20fdff9f3b12a756\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.2887140604010019, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.10494082771571697, \"vector_similarity\": 0.71751827, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-06-28-manual-review-threshold.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e917c6d48a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-06-28-manual-review-threshold.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-06-28-manual-review-threshold.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1695, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:03:51\", \"token_count\": 460, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-MEET-03\\n\\n# Fireflies Transcript: OCR Progress Sync\\n\\n**Date**: 2026-07-05\\n\\n**Participants**: Alice (PM), Bob (Backend), Charlie (Engine), Diana (QA), Evan (DevOps)\\n\\n## Summary\\n\\nCharlie reported the Tesseract OCR fallback is usable but still serial-and-slow on large docs. No redesign this meeting; parallelization deferred until the bottleneck is clearer.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-MEET-03\\n\\n# Fireflies Transcript: OCR Progress Sync\\n\\n**Date**: 2026-07-05\\n\\n**Participants**: Alice (PM), Bob (Backend), Charlie (Engine), Diana (QA), Evan (DevOps)\\n\\n## Transcript\\n\\n**Charlie**: OCR POC update — Tesseract is wired for pages that fail the text-layer path. On large documents it's still slow because we're going page by page in series.\\n\\n**Bob**: Is that good enough to leave in progress, or do we need a redesign now?\\n\\n**Charlie**: Leave it in progress. The POC proves the fallback path. Performance tuning can come once we know where the time actually goes — I don't want to redesign on a guess.\\n\\n**Diana**: I'll keep feeding it the low-confidence pages from the scan samples. Flag anything that looks broken, not just slow.\\n\\n**Alice**: Fine. Charlie stays on the OCR path as ongoing work. We'll revisit parallelization when we have a clearer bottleneck, not today.\\n\\n**Evan**: Nothing from my side until you need a different runtime layout for workers.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src meet 03 firefli transcript ocr progress sync date 2026 07 05 particip alic pm bob backend charli engin diana qa evan devop summari charli report the tesseract ocr fallback is usabl but still serial and slow on larg doc no redesign this meet parallel defer until the bottleneck is clearer sourc id src meet 03 firefli transcript ocr progress sync date 2026 07 05 particip alic pm bob backend charli engin diana qa evan devop transcript charli ocr poc updat tesseract is wire for page that fail the text layer path on larg document it s still slow becaus we re go page by page in seri bob is that good enough to leav in progress or do we need a redesign now charli leav it in progress the poc prof the fallback path perform tune can come onc we know where the time actual go i don t want to redesign on a guess diana i ll keep feed it the low confid page from the scan sampl flag anyth that look broken not just slow alic fine charli stay on the ocr path a ongo work we ll revisit parallel when we have a clearer bottleneck not today evan noth from my side until you need a differ runtim layout for worker\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e94b914e8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/fireflies/2026-07-05-OCR-Progress-Sync.md\", \"id\": \"4b7ee5740decd0a2\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.2800307125416911, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.076148489345273, \"vector_similarity\": 0.7557559, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/fireflies/2026-07-05-OCR-Progress-Sync.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e94b914e8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/fireflies/2026-07-05-OCR-Progress-Sync.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/fireflies/2026-07-05-OCR-Progress-Sync.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1177, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:03:10\", \"token_count\": 344, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-51\\n\\n# Privacy Design Note: Telemetry Opt-Out Flag Semantics\\n\\n**Owner**: Diana\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2051\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-09-06\\n\\n## Opt-Out Behaviour Designed\\n\\nThe CLI and API collect anonymous usage metrics (pages processed, OCR fallback rate) to help tune the detection engine. Setting `CIPHER_TELEMETRY=0`, or the equivalent GUI toggle, is designed to immediately stop all outbound telemetry traffic to the metrics endpoint.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-51\\n\\n# Privacy Design Note: Telemetry Opt-Out Flag Semantics\\n\\n**Owner**: Diana\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2051\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-09-06\\n\\n## Design-Time Issue Found and Patched: Pending-Queue Leak\\n\\nWhile designing the flag semantics, testing surfaced that the opt-out flag blocked network egress correctly, but the `TelemetryLogger` kept writing event payloads to a local SQLite queue regardless. That meant re-enabling telemetry later would flush the entire backlog accumulated during the opt-out period, including events the user believed were never being recorded. The logger was patched to a no-op backend when opted out, closing that gap before the flag semantics were finalized.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-51\\n\\n# Privacy Design Note: Telemetry Opt-Out Flag Semantics\\n\\n**Owner**: Diana\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2051\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-09-06\\n\\n## Verification (Retrospective)\\n\\nA network trace on 2026-08-24 confirmed zero outbound telemetry traffic once the opt-out flag is set, closing the CLI-side verification as Completed.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-51\\n\\n# Privacy Design Note: Telemetry Opt-Out Flag Semantics\\n\\n**Owner**: Diana\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2051\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-09-06\\n\\n## Remaining Limitation\\n\\nThe third-party Electron crash reporter (Sentry) has not been audited for whether it independently respects the opt-out environment variable or requires its own disable hook for minidump uploads.\\n\\n*Note*: CLI-side telemetry opt-out is verified. Full privacy compliance for air-gapped/opt-out users cannot be claimed until the Sentry crash-reporter path is audited separately.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src gdoc 51 privaci design note telemetri opt out flag semant owner diana document key doc 2051 last updat 2026 09 06 opt out behaviour design the cli and api collect anonym usag metric page process ocr fallback rate to help tune the detect engin set cipher _ telemetri 0 or the equival gui toggl is design to immedi stop all outbound telemetri traffic to the metric endpoint sourc id src gdoc 51 privaci design note telemetri opt out flag semant owner diana document key doc 2051 last updat 2026 09 06 design time issu found and patch pend queue leak while design the flag semant test surfac that the opt out flag block network egress correct but the telemetrylogg kept write event payload to a local sqlite queue regardless that meant re enabl telemetri later would flush the entir backlog accumul dure the opt out period includ event the user believ were never be record the logger wa patch to a no op backend when opt out close that gap befor the flag semant were final sourc id src gdoc 51 privaci design note telemetri opt out flag semant owner diana document key doc 2051 last updat 2026 09 06 verif retrospect a network trace on 2026 08 24 confirm zero outbound telemetri traffic onc the opt out flag is set close the cli side verif a complet sourc id src gdoc 51 privaci design note telemetri opt out flag semant owner diana document key doc 2051 last updat 2026 09 06 remain limit the third parti electron crash report sentri ha not been audit for whether it independ respect the opt out environ variabl or requir it own disabl hook for minidump upload note cli side telemetri opt out is verifi full privaci complianc for air gap opt out user can not be claim until the sentri crash report path is audit separ\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e9e43bb08a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-09-06-Telemetry-Opt-Out-Design-and-Compliance-Check.md\", \"id\": \"c3381a6a564a6c9c\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.27746265423997096, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.10023712034281568, \"vector_similarity\": 0.6909889, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-09-06-Telemetry-Opt-Out-Design-and-Compliance-Check.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e9e43bb08a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-09-06-Telemetry-Opt-Out-Design-and-Compliance-Check.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-09-06-Telemetry-Opt-Out-Design-and-Compliance-Check.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1587, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:17\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:00:54\", \"token_count\": 503, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-30\\n\\n# Document: High-DPI-Coordinate-Misalignment-Repro\\n\\n**Owner**: Charlie\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2030\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-09-02 (retrospective, covers 2026-08-17)\\n\\n## Test Logs\\n\\nReproduction notes for the high-DPI coordinate misalignment reported for CIPH-46, first reproduced 2026-08-17.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-30\\n\\n# Document: High-DPI-Coordinate-Misalignment-Repro\\n\\n**Owner**: Charlie\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2030\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-09-02 (retrospective, covers 2026-08-17)\\n\\n## Repro steps\\n\\n1. Open a PDF on a display reporting a scale factor above 1.0 (tested at 150% and 200%).\\n\\n2. Compare the redaction preview overlay's reported box coordinates against the coordinates the rendering library reports for the same region.\\n\\n3. At scale factors above 1.0, the overlay box is offset from the actual text region, with the offset growing as scale factor increases.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-30\\n\\n# Document: High-DPI-Coordinate-Misalignment-Repro\\n\\n**Owner**: Charlie\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2030\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-09-02 (retrospective, covers 202